      "id": "a1-07-1",
      "title": "The verb is always in 2nd place",
      "explanation": [
        "In a normal statement the verb is the **second item**.",
        "**Ek gaan vandag skool toe.** → If you put *vandag* first, the verb still comes second, so the subject moves after it: **Vandag gaan ek skool toe.**",
        "❌ *Vandag ek gaan skool toe.* ✅ **Vandag gaan ek skool toe.**",
        "Going **to** a place: put **toe** after the place: **skool toe** (to school), **huis toe** (home)."
      ],
      "examples": [
        { "af": "Ek speel vandag sokker.", "en": "I'm playing soccer today." },
        { "af": "Vandag speel ek sokker.", "en": "Today I'm playing soccer." },
        { "af": "Môre gaan ons strand toe.", "en": "Tomorrow we're going to the beach." },
        { "af": "Nou eet hulle.", "en": "Now they are eating." }
      ],
      "vocab": ["vandag", "môre", "nou", "toe", "skool", "strand", "gaan", "hier", "daar"],
      "exercises": [
        { "type": "order", "en": "Today I'm playing soccer.", "af": "Vandag speel ek sokker." },
